Triangle $BEO$ is isosceles, so $\angle BEO = \angle EBO = 2y$.  Then $\angle EOD$ is external to triangle $AEO$, so $\angle EOD = \angle EAO + \angle AEO = y + 2y = 3y$.  But $\angle EOD = 45^\circ$, so $\angle BAO = y = 45^\circ/3 = \boxed{15^\circ}$.

